<title>USA: Boston Scientific to shut Denmark plant, cut 240 jobs.</title>
<headline>Boston Scientific to shut Denmark plant, cut 240 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>NATICK, Mass.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boston Scientific Corp., a maker of medical devices, said Thursday it would close its production plant in Stenlose, Denmark, an action that will cut 240 jobs.</p>
<p>Boston Scientific said it was closing the facility as part of the company's strategy to cut costs after several acquisitions in the last two years.</p>
<p>The company was not available for further comment.</p>
<p>The Stenlose facility was acquired as part of Boston Scientific's purchase of Meadox Medicals.</p>
